# Build output and vendored shards. bin/voipappz is ~32MB and regenerated by
# `make cli-build`; lib/ is whatever `shards install` resolved.
#
# shard.lock is NOT here, and that is the point: it pins what lib/ resolves to.
# In va-crystal a repo-wide `shard.lock` rule ignored it while this file claimed
# it was tracked, so it never was — and `mcp` declares no version constraint, so
# every build resolved its HEAD.
/bin/
/lib/
/.shards/
